      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I strongly support this proposal.\n\nI believe giving users control over which worlds they want to see or visit is a much better approach than introducing a Dislike rating system.\n\nUsers should have the freedom to avoid worlds they find uncomfortable, whether because of generative AI, personal experiences, political disagreements, or any other reason. However, their personal choices should not negatively affect a world’s reputation or discoverability for other users.\n\nWorld blocking should remain a personal preference, and the number of blocks should not be used to lower a world’s overall rating or recommendation ranking. Otherwise, it could effectively become another form of Dislike system.\n\nI also appreciate the suggestion to warn users before joining a blocked world while still allowing them to proceed if they choose to.\n\nThis approach would protect individual freedom of choice without encouraging review bombing, retaliation, or unnecessary conflicts between communities.\n\nAnother important advantage is that users can always unblock a world if they change their minds. I believe respecting people’s freedom to reconsider their choices is an essential part of creating a welcoming community.\n\nI believe this would be a healthier and more constructive direction for VRChat.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-10-29T20:05:02.338Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Users should have the freedom to hide content that upsets them, regardless of the context.\n\nGiving users the ability to curate their own worlds tab to hide offensive content places the responsibility and the tools necessary to make choices that can only be made on an individual case-by-case basis in the hands of the individual.\n\nImplementation:\n\nAdd a \"Block World\" button in the list of options when looking at a world on the page that shows instances on the right.\n\nAdd a \"Blocked Worlds\" tab similar to the \"Blocked Users\" tab.\n\nHide the location of any user on Blue or Green who is in a world you've blocked.\n\nWarn users when they are about to accept an invite or join an instance in a world they have blocked.\n\nSpoken Language / Live Play Example:\n\n\"So how would it work if you block a world and you want to join someone who is using that world you blocked, you won't be able to join them or how would this solution work exactly?\"\n\nYour friend, who is on green or blue, will have their location hidden. If you receive or request an invite from that user, you will see the world name appear as normal/part of the invite. When you hit the checkmark to accept the invite, an additional pop-up will appear. \"You are about to join a world you have blocked. Are you sure you want to join?\"",
